  "query_preview": "period of light showers beginning in northern areas during \nthe day Thursday, spreading southeast into the remainder of the \nlower peninsula Friday behind the cold front. Some lake-enhanced \nshowers remain possible behind the front as well, but due to the \nnortherly fetch, most of this lake enhancement will remain over the \nopen waters and along the immediate lakeshore. In any case, rain \namounts throughout this are expected to be very light. Finally, this \nshould bring high temperatures to their lowest point of the next \nweek, with highs dipping into the mid 40s to near 50 degrees. \n\n- More seasonable temperatures this weekend onward\n\nBehind Friday's cold front, much more typical temperatures can be \nexpected over the weekend, as ensemble guidance has trended slightly \ncooler with regard to the post-frontal airmass. In fact, we may see \na localized freeze in many areas Saturday and Sunday mornings, with \nbest chances for a more solid freeze (below 30 degrees) north of the \nM-20 corridor. High temperatures are also expected to remain near \nseasonal averages over the weekend (low to mid 50s). Meanwhile, \nprecipitation chances remain low over the weekend (and beyond), but \nthere remains a slight chance (20%) for some spotty lake-effect rain \nshowers Sunday as a weak shortwave and reinforcing shot of cool air \nmove through the area. In the extended period (Monday onward), a \nslight moderating trend in temperatures appears likely, with minimal \nchances for additional precipitation.",
